module free_call_form.neg_2

// ONE seeded cause: the call passes a RECORD where the function declares an
// `f64`. The arity is right and the name is right; only the type is wrong, and
// the refusal says which of the three it is.
//
// novac ACCEPTED this file until 2026-08-21 and emitted
// `novac_fn_show__nova_f64__to_nova_f64(c)` -- a struct pointer where a double
// is declared, from a program the oracle refuses. The cause was the KEY: the
// call was looked up with `UNKNOWN_TYPE` in every argument slot, so `fits`
// compared the arity and nothing else. Nova overloads BY PARAMETERS (D84), so a
// key without types is not a key at all -- the arguments are typed first now,
// and the walk that types them is also what verifies them.
//
// Kept as a fixture rather than as a note in a commit, because the shape is not
// exotic: any wrong argument is this shape, and a compiler that emits invalid C
// for it says nothing at all.
type Cel { v f64 }

fn show(x f64) -> f64 => x

fn main() {
    ro c = Cel { v: 1.5 }
    println(show(c))
}
